#: ../../adr/0020-feedback-loops.md:1
msgid "ADR-0020: Feedback loops as time iterations of the context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0020-feedback-loops.md:3
msgid "**Status**: accepted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0020-feedback-loops.md:4
msgid "**Date**: 2026-10-18"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0020-feedback-loops.md:5
msgid "**Plan step**: P14.14"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0020-feedback-loops.md:7
msgid "Context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0020-feedback-loops.md:9
msgid ""
"Adaptive optics, servo loops and iterative calibrations feed a "
"measurement back to an actuator. REQ-CTX-2 keeps the graph of signals "
"acyclic and asks that \"physical loops (AO, servo, iterative calibration)"
" are time iterations driven by the context\". Until now LUMOS had the "
"pieces (time-dependent turbulence, a deformable mirror with a `commands` "
"state, an ideal modal correction inside `Atmosphere`) but no way to close"
" a loop: a review of the web interface (18/10/2026) asked for an adaptive"
" optics preset with a real feedback loop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0020-feedback-loops.md:15
msgid "Decision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0020-feedback-loops.md:17
msgid ""
"**Feedbacks** connect an output port to a field of an element: "
"`ctx.feedback(\"ctrl.commands\", \"dm.commands\", mode=\"add\")`. They "
"are not connections of the graph (which stays acyclic): they are applied "
"*between* two iterations, so a loop always has at least one frame of "
"delay, as a real loop. Two modes: `\"set\"` (the field takes the value of"
" the port) and `\"add\"` (the value is added: an integrator whose gain is"
" in the element that computes the correction). The value of the port is a"
" `DataProduct` (or a quantity) of the unit and shape of the field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0020-feedback-loops.md:23
msgid ""
"**`ctx.loop(steps, period=..., outputs=...)`** runs the context `steps` "
"times: compute the outputs and the sources of the feedbacks at time "
"`t_k`, apply the feedbacks, advance the clock by `period`. It returns one"
" `LoopStep(step, time, outputs)` per iteration; the states written by the"
" feedbacks and the clock are kept (the loop has run), unless "
"`restore=True`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0020-feedback-loops.md:27
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Feedbacks are saved in `.lumos` documents (top-level `\"feedbacks\": "
"[{\"from\", \"to\", \"mode\"}]`), which makes the format **1.1**; LUMOS "
"reads 1.0 and 1.1 documents, a 1.0 reader refuses 1.1 documents instead "
"of dropping the loops silently. `ctx.to_python()` writes "
"`ctx.feedback(...)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0020-feedback-loops.md:30
msgid ""
"Adaptive optics elements: `WavefrontSensor`, an ideal Shack-Hartmann "
"(mean gradient of the optical path in square sub-apertures, from the "
"phase differences of neighbouring pixels, so that large wrapped phases "
"are measured; plus the RMS residual of the optical path, valid below "
"about λ/4), and `AOController`, an integrator `Δc = -g R s` whose "
"reconstructor `R` is the regularised pseudo-inverse of the interaction "
"matrix of a deformable mirror of the same geometry (computed analytically"
" from the separable influence functions). A source element may check its "
"feedback targets (`check_feedback`): the controller refuses a mirror of "
"another geometry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0020-feedback-loops.md:37
msgid ""
"The service runs a loop as a job (`run_loop`, kind `loop`); its steps are"
" read like the points of a study (`get_study`, parameters `time`), so "
"that the web interface and assistants plot and export them the same way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0020-feedback-loops.md:41
msgid "Alternatives considered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0020-feedback-loops.md:43
msgid ""
"Cycles in the graph with a delay element: the planner, the caching of "
"results and the validation assume an acyclic graph (ADR-0006); a cycle "
"would need a fixed-point semantics everywhere for one use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0020-feedback-loops.md:45
msgid ""
"Callbacks in Python between runs: not serialisable, not available from "
"the web interface or to assistants."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0020-feedback-loops.md:46
msgid ""
"A single \"AO system\" element (sensor, controller and mirror together): "
"simpler for one use, but hides the loop and does not extend to servo "
"loops, calibrations or bench actuators."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0020-feedback-loops.md:49
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0020-feedback-loops.md:51
msgid ""
"Loops are explicit, saved, undoable in the service, and available in "
"Python, in the web interface and to assistants."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0020-feedback-loops.md:53
msgid ""
"Every loop has a delay of one period at least; shorter latencies are "
"modelled by a smaller period."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0020-feedback-loops.md:54
msgid ""
"The controller repeats the geometry of its mirror (checked when the loop "
"starts). Other controllers (modal, predictive) and sensors (pyramid, "
"noise of the sensor) can follow the same pattern."
msgstr ""

